{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ערות אביך וערות אמך", :translit "ervot avicha v'ervot imecha", :gloss "the nakedness of your father and the nakedness of your mother"} {:he "כי שלשה שותפין יש באדם", :translit "ki shlosha shutafin yesh ba'adam", :gloss "for there are three partners in a person"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse mentions both father and mother, alluding to the three-partner tradition: God, father, and mother."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states there are three partners in a person — the Holy One, the father, and the mother. The father contributes the white substances (bones, sinews, nails, brain, white of the eye) and the mother contributes the red substances (skin, flesh, blood, hair, dark of the eye), while God provides the spirit, soul, facial appearance, vision, hearing, speech, and the ability to walk (Niddah 31a). Since the verse mentions both father and mother together, Ba'al HaTurim reads it as an allusion to this three-partner framework.", :sources ["Niddah 31a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse mentions both father and mother, alluding to the three-partner tradition: God, father, and mother.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:58.829778913Z", :model "glm-5.2"}